  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "This recipe calls for asian eggplants, or Japanese eggplants. They are long and thin compared to a European or globe eggplant, and much more tender and delicate. If you can't find them you can substitute globe eggplant, but the dish is really best with the asian eggplant."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "*A lot of grocery stores have Asian ingredient aisles now. You should be able to find chili-bean paste, a mixture of preserved chilies mixed with mashed soybeans, there or at any Asian market. (Do not confuse with black bean paste or chili-garlic paste.)",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "6c12a339-683b-5653-9552-b1e10c050553"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "**Sichuan peppercorns are available at some stores and online for quite cheap. They aren't spicy like other peppers but rather have a citrusy flavor and induce a tingly, numbing sensation like a carbonated drink."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "Prep eggplant, chili sauce, cornstarch slurry, vinegar and scallions:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "dd1435a0-f330-5a09-bb1c-093cd8cd27ea",
        "e7e140d4-2f1c-5f08-9f79-a764ec77a8a6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 5,
      "instruction": "Begin your mise en place. Quarter the eggplant lengthwise and chop into large batons and set aside."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 6,
      "instruction": "In a small bowl, mix together the chicken stock, sugar, and soy sauce and set it aside.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "7848fd0a-6e5f-5f6b-92e0-fa2eaa20c931",
        "4883be85-0ee1-538c-9bce-04044df72347",
        "f724bf6f-1153-5ddf-9cf9-e7f2ff4eee1e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 7,
      "instruction": "In a second bowl, mix together the chili bean paste, garlic, ginger, and sichuan peppercorns and set it aside.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "7e03fb8f-ad46-5d2d-9441-591814c8d62d",
        "6c12a339-683b-5653-9552-b1e10c050553"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 8,
      "instruction": "In a third bowl, mix together the cornstarch with a tablespoon of water and set it aside.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "dd1435a0-f330-5a09-bb1c-093cd8cd27ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 9,
      "instruction": "Lastly, in a fourth bowl, mix together the scallions and vinegar and set it aside.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "e7e140d4-2f1c-5f08-9f79-a764ec77a8a6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 10,
      "instruction": "Sauté eggplant:"
    },
    {
      "step_number": 11,
      "instruction": "Place the oil in a wok or large sauté pan over medium-high heat until the oil is almost smoking. Add the eggplant and sauté, allowing it to sit for a few seconds each time you move it to allow it to brown and blister. If the eggplant absorbs all the oil and some pieces don't get any then add a little more oil."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 12,
      "instruction": "Add the chili bean paste, garlic, ginger, and sichuan peppercorns and sauté:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "7e03fb8f-ad46-5d2d-9441-591814c8d62d",
        "6c12a339-683b-5653-9552-b1e10c050553"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 13,
      "instruction": "until fragrant, about 30 seconds.",
      "timer_seconds": 30
    },
    {
      "step_number": 14,
      "instruction": "Add the chicken stock mixture:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "7848fd0a-6e5f-5f6b-92e0-fa2eaa20c931"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 15,
      "instruction": "turn the heat to medium-low and simmer for 90 seconds.",
      "timer_seconds": 90
    },
    {
      "step_number": 16,
      "instruction": "Add the cornstarch mixture:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "dd1435a0-f330-5a09-bb1c-093cd8cd27ea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 17,
      "instruction": "and stir together until the sauce thickens a bit."
    },
    {
      "step_number": 18,
      "instruction": "Add the scallions and vinegar:",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "e7e140d4-2f1c-5f08-9f79-a764ec77a8a6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 19,
      "instruction": "and cook for 15 seconds to diffuse their harsh flavors a bit.",
      "timer_seconds": 15
    },
    {
      "step_number": 20,
      "instruction": "Garnish with cilantro and serve.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "76a56283-76cc-5e8c-a722-bfa914383530"
      ]
    }
  ],
